sections.text:
For purposes of this Ordinance, the following terms shall mean:

(a) Closed-Circuit Television (CCTV) System - refers to a video surveillance system in which signals are transmitted to monitors and recording devices within a closed network;

(b) Commercial Establishment - refers to banks, shopping malls, supermarkets, hotels, restaurants, bars, pawnshops, and business establishments operating in Davao City;

(c) Public and Common Areas - refers to entry and exit doors, lobbies, parking areas, and transaction counters accessible to the general public;

(d) PSSO - refers to the Public Safety and Security Office of the City Government of Davao.

Any establishment or person violating this Ordinance shall, upon conviction, be penalized as follows:

(a) First Offense: A fine of One Thousand Pesos (Php 1,000.00);

(b) Second Offense: A fine of Three Thousand Pesos (Php 3,000.00);

(c) Third and Subsequent Offenses: A fine of Five Thousand Pesos (Php 5,000.00) and revocation of Mayor's Business Permit until full compliance is certified.
